---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---
<SiteLayout title="About" active="about">
  <section class="page-intro wrap"><p class="eyebrow">02 / ABOUT SHASHI</p><div class="page-intro-row"><h1>Reliable by<br />design.<br /><em>Curious by default.</em></h1><p>I’m {site.name}, a backend-focused developer based in {site.location}. I build the services and integrations that help products and business operations work reliably.</p></div></section>
  <section class="about-profile wrap"><div class="profile-art"><div class="profile-initials">S<span>K</span></div><span class="mono">A PORTRAIT CAN GO HERE</span></div><div class="about-copy"><p class="eyebrow">BACKEND ENGINEERING · APPLIED AI</p><h2>Build the system.<br />Keep learning.</h2><p>My work centers on Node.js, TypeScript, APIs, databases, and asynchronous workflows. I’ve built e-commerce integrations, data migration pipelines, warehouse tools, and operational automation.</p><p>I’m also learning AI and building products with AI agents. I’m interested in how agent-based systems can become useful products, with dependable backend foundations behind them.</p><a class="text-link" href="/ai/">EXPLORE MY AI LEARNING <span>↗</span></a></div></section>
  <section class="principles wrap"><div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">HOW I APPROACH THE WORK</p><span class="mono">ENGINEERING PRINCIPLES</span></div><div class="principle-row"><span>01</span><h3>Make data dependable.</h3><p>Build clear data flows, validation, and recovery paths so systems can stay in sync.</p></div><div class="principle-row"><span>02</span><h3>Design for real operations.</h3><p>Understand the business rules behind a workflow and turn them into useful services and tools.</p></div><div class="principle-row"><span>03</span><h3>Keep learning by building.</h3><p>Explore new ideas through working prototypes, including products built with AI agents.</p></div></section>
  <section class="experience wrap"><div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">EXPERIENCE</p><span class="mono">FROM MY RÉSUMÉ</span></div>{site.experience.map((item) => <div class="experience-row"><span>{item.dates}</span><strong>{item.title}</strong><span>{item.organization} · {item.location}</span></div>)}<div class="experience-row"><span>{site.education.dates}</span><strong>{site.education.title}</strong><span>{site.education.organization} · {site.education.location}</span></div></section>
</SiteLayout>
